# `dist/` is build output that is compared BYTE FOR BYTE.
#
# The monorepo's `check:published-dist` gate fingerprints these files and
# requires them to equal a fresh `ncc` build of packages/github-action. Git's
# end-of-line conversion would rewrite index.js and index.js.map in a working
# copy on a platform whose native ending is CRLF, and a re-commit from that
# copy would ship a bundle whose bytes no longer match any build. Committing
# the current bundle already produced the warning:
#
#   in the working copy of 'dist/index.js', LF will be replaced by CRLF
#
# `-text` turns the conversion off in both directions, so the bytes here are
# the bytes that were built.
dist/** -text
